🥥 did you know?
   └─ rhx git.package.patch set --package <name> --mode apply
"
`;

exports[`git.package.patch.sh given: [case4] the dispatcher when: [t3] a flag is given with no value then: set (seal) refuses loud, never a silent exit 1`] = `
"🐢 bummer dude...

🐚 git.package.patch set
   └─ ✋ ConstraintError: --why is required

🥥 did you know?
   ├─ add --why '<why this patch is needed>', or pipe it via --why @stdin
   └─ rhx git.package.patch set --package is-number --why '<why>' --upstream '<issue-url>' --mode apply
"
`;

exports[`git.package.patch.sh given: [case4] the dispatcher when: [t4] a subcommand help is asked for then: get --help names --when and each state 1`] = `
"🐢 heres the wave...

🐚 git.package.patch get
   ├─ usage
   │  └─ rhx git.package.patch get [--when hook.onStop]
   ├─ flags
   │  └─ --when   (optional) hook.onStop: nudge only, always exit 0, silent when naught is owed
   ├─ states
   │  ├─ applied        the installed copy holds the patch
   │  ├─ unapplied      the entry is recorded, but pnpm has not applied it yet
   │  ├─ underapplied   the installed version moved, or a hunk no longer fits
   │  ├─ obsolete       the installed version already holds the change
   │  ├─ unused         the package is no longer installed
   │  ├─ unbacked       an entry names a patch file that is absent
   │  └─ unrecorded     a patch file no entry records
   └─ examples
      ├─ rhx git.package.patch get
      └─ rhx git.package.patch get --when hook.onStop
"
`;

exports[`git.package.patch.sh given: [case4] the dispatcher when: [t4] a subcommand help is asked for then: set --help names both phases and each flag, required or optional, with defaults 1`] = `
"🐢 heres the wave...

🐚 git.package.patch set
   ├─ usage
   │  ├─ rhx git.package.patch set --package <name>[@<version>] [--edit-dir <dir>] [--mode plan|apply]
   │  └─ rhx git.package.patch set --package <name>[@<version>] --why '<why>' --upstream '<issue-url>' [--edit-dir <dir>] [--mode plan|apply]
   ├─ phases
   │  ├─ open   no --why, no --upstream: open an in-tree edit dir, with any committed patch laid on it
   │  └─ seal   --why + --upstream: seal the edit dir into patches/<name>@<version>.patch + its note
   ├─ flags
   │  ├─ --package    (required) the dependency, bare or @<version>
   │  ├─ --why        (seal) why the patch exists; @stdin reads it from a pipe
   │  ├─ --upstream   (seal) the http(s) link where the upstream fix is queued
   │  ├─ --edit-dir   (optional) an in-tree dir; default node_modules/.pnpm_patches/<name>@<version>
   │  └─ --mode       (optional) plan (default) or apply
   └─ examples
      ├─ rhx git.package.patch set --package rhachet --mode apply
      ├─ rhx git.package.patch set --package rhachet --why 'keep the stop hook quiet on a clean tree' --upstream https://github.com/ehmpathy/rhachet/issues/580 --mode apply
      └─ printf 'keep the stop hook quiet' | rhx git.package.patch set --package rhachet --why @stdin --upstream https://github.com/ehmpathy/rhachet/issues/580 --mode apply
"
`;

exports[`git.package.patch.sh given: [case5] a dir whose repo shape the verb refuses when: [t0] the cwd is not inside a git repo then: set (open) is refused 1`] = `
